The Cybersalt Digest – Issue #3448

*****************

*Cybersalt Beat*

Sunday greetings, happy 10-10-10, and a blessed Thanksgiving to everyone in
Canada!

There is a new devotional on the Cybersalt site today. You can read James
Snyder's "Home has Never Been Sweeter" at:
http://www.cybersalt.org/featured-blogs/gods-penman/5376

Last week's service and sermon at Westside Bible Church have not yet been
put on the site, but I have fixed the Twitter auto-update on the Westside
site so if you use twitter and follow westsidefamily you'll be tweeted as
soon as those are added.

Enjoy the rest of today's digest. 
*******************

Here is today's CleanLaugh. - Landing in the Fog

An airliner is coming into land at an airport obscured by fog.  Visibility
is practically nil, the ILS system is on the blink, so the pilot has to
land on wits alone.  "Flaps, check," he says to the co-pilot, "Landing
Gear, check. Altitude, check. Right, we're going in. Hold on." 

The plane lands and comes to a screeching, grinding halt; just short of the
edge of the runway.  "Wow!" exclaims the pilot, "This must be the shortest
runway I've ever landed on!" 

The co-pilot looks left and right and says "Yeah, and about the widest,
too..."

You can rate this joke at:
http://www.cybersalt.org/cleanlaugh-archive/5375

